    "problem_statement": "# Retry mechanism broken in tenacity\n\nI've found an issue with the retry mechanism in tenacity. When using retry with certain configurations, it fails to work properly.\n\nHere's a simple reproduction case:\n\n```python\nfrom tenacity import retry, stop_after_attempt\n\n@retry(stop=stop_after_attempt(3))\ndef my_function():\n    print(\"Attempt\")\n    raise ValueError(\"This should be retried\")\n\ntry:\n    my_function()\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print(f\"Got exception: {type(e).__name__}\")\n```\n\nExpected behavior:\n- The function should print \"Attempt\" three times\n- Then raise a RetryError with the original ValueError as the cause\n\nActual behavior:\n- The function only runs once\n- The retry mechanism doesn't work properly\n- Instead of getting a RetryError, we get a different error or unexpected behavior\n\nI also noticed issues with the before_sleep callback not being called properly:\n\n```python\ndef log_sleep(retry_state):\n    print(f\"Sleeping for {retry_state.upcoming_sleep} seconds\")\n\n@retry(stop=stop_after_attempt(3), before_sleep=log_sleep)\ndef my_function():\n    print(\"Attempt\")\n    raise ValueError(\"This should be retried\")\n\ntry:\n    my_function()\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print(f\"Got exception: {type(e).__name__}\")\n```\n\nThe before_sleep callback isn't being called as expected.\n\nThis seems to be related to changes in the `_post_stop_check_actions` method. The retry mechanism isn't properly handling the retry state and actions.\n\n<END WRITING>"
  },
